#: README.md:226
msgid ""
"[!IMPORTANT] <span id=\"transitions-discussion\">Many transitions are "
"observed, which is a good sign, but is not sufficient for building a "
"converged free energy. Counting the number of back and forth transition is "
"in fact a deceiving criterium for convergence. It is true that back and "
"forth transitions are necessary for building a free energy as one must "
"sample well the relevant phase space. However, if those transitions are due "
"to an out-of-equilibrium bias potential that strongly changes in time, the "
"reweight procedure would be noisy, ineffective and overall ill-defined. One "
"must have back and forth transitions _and_ a quasi-static underlying bias "
"potential to build a converged FES. </span>"
msgstr ""
"[!IMPORTANT] <span id=\"transitions-"
"discussion\">多数の往復遷移はよい兆候ですが、収束には不十分です。重要な Phase Space の Sampling "
"に必要ですが、時間変化の大きい非平衡 Bias による遷移なら、Reweighting は Noisy で非効率、定義も不明瞭になります。収束した "
"FES には往復遷移 _と_ 準静的 BiasPotential が必要です。</span>"

